{{Quote|The only thing more powerful than knowledge is a loaded rocket launcher.|[[Hondo Ohnaka's mother]], as quoted by her [[Hondo Ohnaka|son]]|<ref name="Secrets Bounty Hunters">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Bounty Hunters]]''</ref>}}
'''Missile launchers''', also known as '''rocket launchers''' or '''warhead launchers''', were a class of weapon which launched [[Missile|explosive projectiles]]. Launchers ranged in size and function, from small weapons usable by a single individual<ref name="Ambush">{{TCW|Ambush}}</ref> to larger launchers which were built into [[starship]]s such as the [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]],<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|republic-attack-gunship|Republic Attack Gunship}}</ref> or ground vehicles like the [[All Terrain Missile Platform]].<ref name="SWC">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> They saw use during the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Ambush" /> and the subsequent [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="SWC" />

==History==
During the [[Clone Wars]] the [[clone trooper]]s of the [[Galactic Republic]] used [[RPS-6 rocket launcher]]s.<ref name="RPS-6 Rocket Launcher Databank">{{Databank|rps-6-rocket-launcher|RPS-6 Rocket Launcher}}</ref>

During the Galactic Civil War, [[technician]]s with the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] began manufacturing launchers that were quicker to reload. These launchers were often stolen by [[pirate]]s and installed on their ships in order to boost their firepower.<ref name="Outlaws" /> In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> [[merchant]]s affiliated with the [[Miyuki Trade League]] sold these improved launchers for 2250 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]].<ref name="Outlaws" />
{{Gamemechanics|canon=1}}
In 3 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate" /> the [[Scoundrel/Legends|scoundrel]] [[Kay Vess]] purchased these improved launchers for use on the ''[[Trailblazer]]'', her [[EML-850 light freighter]].<ref name="Outlaws" />
{{Endgame}}

